# Optional organization restriction only. Leave UNSET for safe custom public HTTPS APIs.
# CHAT3D_ALLOWED_UPSTREAMS=https://approved-provider.example/v1
# Never put API keys in VITE_* variables, source files or Docker images.
# Behind an HTTPS reverse proxy set the external page origin:
# CHAT3D_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://chat3d.example.com
# Optional Node-only copy of the same Tauri latest.json. Not the desktop client's URL.
# CHAT3D_DESKTOP_UPDATE_MANIFEST=/opt/1panel/www/sites/portal.jiezi-ai.com/index/desktop-updates/chat3d/latest.json
# Build-time release notes baked into dist/version.json and the desktop manifest. Do not put secrets here:
# CHAT3D_UPDATE_NOTES=
# CHAT3D_UPDATE_PUB_DATE=2026-10-26T00:00:00Z
# Desktop release build only. Public values; keep the private key out of the repo.
# Portal static manifest (origin listens on 38008 behind Cloudflare Tunnel):
# CHAT3D_UPDATER_ENDPOINT=https://portal.jiezi-ai.com/desktop-updates/chat3d/latest.json
# CHAT3D_UPDATER_PUBKEY=
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY=
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD=
